","urn:sfpl:31223074134561","urn:bwbsku:O6-BTU-011"],"physical_format":"Hardcover","ia_loaded_id":["lifeafterdeathbu00chop"],"key":"/books/OL9800054M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL39038A","name":"Deepak Chopra"}],"ocaid":"lifeafterdeathbu00chop","isbn_13":["9780307345783"],"source_records":["amazon:0307345785:2-au:2272369603:256780","marc:marc_loc_updates/v35.i17.records.utf8:6539204:2569","marc:CollingswoodLibraryMarcDump10-27-2008/Collingswood.out:70892108:2391","ia:lifeafterdeathbu00chop","marc:marc_openlibraries_sanfranciscopubliclibrary/sfpl_chq_2018_12_24_run03.mrc:157049336:3678","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part33.utf8:108051950:2569","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-04-09","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.10.20150123.full.mrc:89943200:2144","ia:lifeafterdeathbu0000chop_v9v8"],"title":"Life After Death","number_of_pages":304,"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"subjects":["God (Theology)","Religion","Psychology","Death, Grief, Bereavement","Self-Help / General","Christian Theology - General","Eschatology","Metaphysics","Future life"],"publish_date":"October 17, 2006","works":[{"key":"/works/OL548752W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"9.3 x 6.4 x 1.2 inches","lccn":["2006013853"],"lc_classifications":["BL535 .C535 2006"],"oclc_numbers":["68133044"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"Chopra turns to the most profound mystery: what happens after we die? Is this one question we were not meant to answer, a riddle whose solution the universe keeps to itself? Chopra tells us there is abundant evidence that \"the world beyond\" is not separated from this world by an impassable wall; in fact, a single reality embraces all worlds, all times and places. At the end of our lives we \"cross over\" into a new phase of the same soul journey we are on right this minute. Chopra draws on cutting-edge scientific discoveries and the great wisdom traditions to provide a map of the afterlife. It's a journey into many levels of consciousness. But more important is his urgent message: Who you meet in the afterlife and what you experience there reflect your present beliefs, expectations, and level of awareness. Here and now, you shape what happens after you die.--From publisher description."},"latest_revision":19,"revision":19,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-09-16T04:31:10.044570"}}},"ISBN:9780674064003":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780674064003","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18360588M/The_Beginnings_of_Indian_philosophy","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL18360588M/The_Beginnings_of_Indian_philosophy","details":{"publishers":["Harvard University Press"],"subtitle":"selections from the Rig Veda, Atharva Veda, Upanisads, and Mahabharata","key":"/books/OL18360588M","publish_places":["Cambridge, MA"],"contributions":["Edgerton, Franklin."],"source_records":["marc:talis_openlibrary_contribution/talis-openlibrary-contribution.mrc:1810210229:647","bwb:9780674064003","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2020-10-07"],"title":"The Beginnings of Indian philosophy","dewey_decimal_class":["294.592"],"identifiers":{"librarything":["1376032"],"goodreads":["381028"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"isbn_10":["0674064003"],"publish_date":"1965","publish_country":"xxu","by_statement":"translated from the Sanskrit with an introduction, notes and glossarial index by Franklin Edgerton.","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2606714W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"local_id":["urn:bwbsku:P3-ANK-737"],"latest_revision":7,"revision":7,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-10-16T09:21:37.853636"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2024-01-30T23:48:00.428563"}}},"ISBN:9781852692889":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781852692889","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL17520322M/Lights_for_Gita","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL17520322M/Lights_for_Gita","deta